For the situation of highly automated driving and non-drivingrelated activities, we see many questions which have to be investigated. With the results of our experiments we hope to provide a basis for the design of future non-driving-related activities in highly automated cars. These activities show the potential of the car as a novel space for the consumption of mobile and ubiquitous multimedia applications.
